raft will join the fleet  this year and it plans to gradually  reposition the existing wide-body  dreamliner fleet to western canada where  its most popular routes are add more  non-stop direct flights between western  canadian communities while maintaining a  presence in eastern provinces but the  airline hasn't established exactly what  it means for routes and prices it's  clear air canada dominates the east and  easterners for some reason have a  wedding or a love affair with air canada  and i think westjet finds it very  difficult to penetrate that market  for the airlines that are left traveling  to those destinations  they can easily raise  fares  and that's not good for the consumer  everybody is looking for a deal  now from the west to the east  there'll be no deals  it'll be just full fair it'll be fairs  that people cannot afford  but industry experts say while the  pandemic has taken its toll westjet's  biggest issue is complexity operating  multiple aircraft types and after buying  ultra low cost carrier swoop if you look  at the most successful airlines in the  planet from a profitability standpoint  they're probably southwest and and  someone like ryanair and what do they  have in common they only have one  aircraft type they only fly the 737 so  every pilot can fly every airplane which  is how westjet once operated i think  it's great i think westjet needs to  compete a little bit in the low fare  department especially with the likes of  flare and swoop that are taking over so  amid high fuel prices and economic  uncertainty as demand recovers in a  vastly different landscape for this  airline its strategy is going back to  the future nitu garcia global news  that's global national for this friday  night i'm farin asser and i want to  thank you so much for spending part of  your evening with us tonight's your  canada is the halifax skyline we love  seeing your canada so please keep  sending us those photos to viewers at  globalnational.com  until tomo